; The Tipshop is a useful cross-check (TAKE vs GET). Not
; playthrough-verified.

[Solution:overview:Overview]

Escape the damaged city, bridge the chasm, and restart the reactor
backup systems.

Primary route: Classic Adventures Solution Archive file id 14
(https://solutionarchive.com/file/id,14/). Compass runs written as
Ex3/Wx3 in that file are expanded here to E, E, E / W, W, W. Millard
notes the Spectrum version prefers TAKE over GET.

#LIST
{ Carry TV (or radio) for looters; do not carry it past the soldiers }
{ Many red herrings - ignore them }
LIST#

[Solution:notes-redherrings:Red Herrings]

CASA lists: pen, radio, desk, tissues, pickaxe, diamond, stick, cap,
trumpet, ticket, sweets and rusty nail. Tom Hayes's longer CASA FAQ
(file id 8051) and Dorothy Millard's Tipshop walkthrough expand
individual puzzles if this short route loses you.

[Solution:notes-hazards:Carry Rules]

Tips: to pass soldiers on Manor Drive, do not carry the television; to
cross waste ground / satisfy looters, do carry the television (or
radio). Drop it once the looters are gone.

